```plaintext
Scene Description in RDF Triples (Turtle Format)
```

```turtle
@prefix ex: <http://example.org/autonomous-driving#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

ex:Scene1 a ex:DrivingScene ;
    ex:hasWeatherCondition ex:FoggyCondition ;
    ex:hasTimeOfDay ex:Daytime .

ex:FoggyCondition a ex:WeatherCondition ;
    rdfs:label "Fog" .

ex:Vehicle1 a ex:Vehicle ;
    ex:hasPosition ex:Position1 ;
    ex:hasType "Sedan" ;
    ex:hasColor "Dark" ;
    ex:isFollowing ex:Vehicle2 .

ex:Vehicle2 a ex:Vehicle ;
    ex:hasPosition ex:Position2 ;
    ex:hasType "Sedan" ;
    ex:hasColor "Dark" ;
    ex:isApproaching ex:Intersection .

ex:Position1 a ex:Position ;
    ex:hasCoordinates "Near, RightLane, 100m" .

ex:Position2 a ex:Position ;
    ex:hasCoordinates "Far, CenterLane, 200m" .

ex:Intersection a ex:RoadInfrastructure ;
    ex:hasType "FourWay" ;
    ex:hasTrafficSign ex:TrafficSign1 .

ex:TrafficSign1 a ex:TrafficSign ;
    ex:hasType "Stop" ;
    ex:isOccludedBy ex:FoggyCondition .

ex:RoadInfrastructure1 a ex:RoadInfrastructure ;
    ex:hasType "RoadMarking" ;
    ex:hasPattern "ArrowRight" .

ex:Building1 a ex:Building ;
    ex:hasPosition ex:Position3 ;
    ex:isOccluding ex:Vehicle2 .

ex:Position3 a ex:Position ;
    ex:hasCoordinates "LeftSide, 50m" .

ex:Building2 a ex:Building ;
    ex:hasPosition ex:Position4 ;
    ex:isOccluding ex:TrafficSign1 .

ex:Position4 a ex:Position ;
    ex:hasCoordinates "RightSide, 150m" .
```

---

```plaintext
Identified Risks for each risk class
```

**Risk 1:**
Description: Reduced visibility due to fog, leading to potential misidentification or delayed detection of vehicles, pedestrians, and traffic signs.
Severity Score: 0.85

**Risk 2:**
Description: Occlusion of traffic signs by fog and buildings, increasing the risk of misinterpreting road rules and traffic instructions.
Severity Score: 0.75

**Risk 3:**
Description: Vehicle following too closely in low-visibility conditions, increasing the risk of rear-end collisions.
Severity Score: 0.70

**Risk 4:**
Description: Potential for vehicles to misjudge distances and speeds in foggy conditions, leading to unsafe maneuvers at intersections.
Severity Score: 0.80

**Risk 5:**
Description: Inability to detect pedestrians or cyclists due to low visibility, increasing the risk of collisions with vulnerable road users.
Severity Score: 0.90

**Risk 6:**
Description: Misinterpretation of road markings due to fog, leading to incorrect lane changes or turns.
Severity Score: 0.70

---
The severity scores are based on a scale where 0 is no risk and 1 is an imminent risk of collision or severe accident. The scores reflect the potential danger in this specific foggy environment.